WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.699
I woke up on Saturday morning with a big smile on my face.

2
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.803
What was I smiling about? I wondered.

3
00:00:09.804 --> 00:00:11.914
Then I remembered.

4
00:00:11.915 --> 00:00:15.802
Today I was going to move into my own room!

5
00:00:15.803 --> 00:00:21.026
I'd never have to share a room with my brother, Tate, again.

6
00:00:21.027 --> 00:00:22.957
I went into the kitchen.

7
00:00:22.958 --> 00:00:28.159
My mom had left a note that said she was grocery shopping.

8
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.867
I ate breakfast and then went back to our room.

9
00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:35.027
By now Tate was awake.

10
00:00:35.028 --> 00:00:39.451
He watched me dump all my stuff in a big box.

11
00:00:39.452 --> 00:00:43.545
"Good-bye, Tate," I said, picking up the box.

12
00:00:43.546 --> 00:00:48.196
Tate grinned. "See you around, Iggy."

13
00:00:48.197 --> 00:00:51.655
I could tell that Tate was happy I was leaving.

14
00:00:51.656 --> 00:00:55.784
But I didn't mind, because I was happy too.

15
00:00:55.785 --> 00:00:59.489
My new room was a tiny space off the kitchen.

16
00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:07.827
Mr. Calabria, the superintendent of our apartment building, had built shelves for all my invention stuff.

17
00:01:07.828 --> 00:01:11.665
Soon he was going to move my bed into the room too.

18
00:01:11.666 --> 00:01:15.595
"Hey, Iggy!" Tate yelled. "Come back here!"

19
00:01:15.596 --> 00:01:21.413
"Wow," I thought in surprise. "Tate misses me already!"

20
00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.636
I walked back to Tate's room.

21
00:01:23.637 --> 00:01:26.395
"What do you want?" I asked.

22
00:01:26.396 --> 00:01:29.160
"You forgot something," said Tate.

23
00:01:29.161 --> 00:01:32.379
He pointed under his desk.

24
00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:36.875
I looked, but I couldn't see anything.

25
00:01:36.876 --> 00:01:40.291
"There's a broken crayon under there," Tate said.

26
00:01:40.292 --> 00:01:45.128
I looked again and spotted a tiny piece of broken crayon.

27
00:01:45.129 --> 00:01:48.698
It was from the automatic coloring machine I'd invented.

28
00:01:48.699 --> 00:01:52.076
I picked it up and then went to the door.

29
00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:55.508
Mr. Calabria was here to move my bed.

30
00:01:55.509 --> 00:01:59.836
I was still setting up my new room when Mom got home.

31
00:01:59.837 --> 00:02:04.040
"I'm so tired from shopping," she said.

32
00:02:04.041 --> 00:02:10.145
"After I put these groceries away, I'm going to sit down with a good book."

33
00:02:10.146 --> 00:02:13.903
Just then someone knocked on our apartment door.

34
00:02:13.904 --> 00:02:17.649
It was my friend Molly, who lives across the hall.

35
00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.769
Her little brother, Caswell, was with her.

36
00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:25.603
"Hi, Iggy," she said. "How's your new room?"

37
00:02:25.604 --> 00:02:32.804
"I'm almost all moved in," I said. "Come and see!"

38
00:02:32.805 --> 00:02:36.398
I showed them my new room.

39
00:02:36.399 --> 00:02:39.242
"I'm going to think up great inventions here.

40
00:02:39.243 --> 00:02:41.638
My next invention will be healthy candy.

41
00:02:41.639 --> 00:02:44.489
You two can help."

42
00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:46.310
Molly made a face.

43
00:02:46.311 --> 00:02:49.391
"Who wants to eat healthy candy?"

44
00:02:49.392 --> 00:02:52.844
"We're not going to eat it," I explained.

45
00:02:52.845 --> 00:02:54.596
"We're going to sell it!

46
00:02:54.597 --> 00:02:59.044
Moms will buy it for their kids."

47
00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:01.318
I went back into the kitchen.

48
00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:06.427
"Mom, can we use some frozen vegetables for my new invention?"

49
00:03:06.428 --> 00:03:11.290
"Okay," she said. "But don't make a mess."

50
00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:16.465
"I won't," I promised. Then I got busy.

51
00:03:16.466 --> 00:03:21.303
First I took three bags of frozen vegetables out of the freezer.

52
00:03:21.304 --> 00:03:25.215
There were lima beans, peas, and broccoli.

53
00:03:25.216 --> 00:03:29.563
Next I dumped the vegetables on a platter in my room.

54
00:03:29.564 --> 00:03:33.286
The broccoli was all stuck together.

55
00:03:33.287 --> 00:03:36.705
We had to use a hammer to break it apart.

56
00:03:36.706 --> 00:03:41.620
"This is fun!" said Caswell, pounding the frozen broccoli.

57
00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:45.733
"But how are we going to make candy?" asked Molly.

58
00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:49.281
"You'll see," I told her.

59
00:03:49.282 --> 00:03:52.226
I went into the kitchen and got a stool.

60
00:03:52.227 --> 00:03:55.718
Then I climbed up and got a bottle from the cupboard.

61
00:03:55.719 --> 00:03:59.757
Its label said "Chocolate Syrup."

62
00:03:59.758 --> 00:04:04.379
"Now," I said, as I came back into my room.

63
00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:07.837
"We'll pour the syrup over the frozen vegetables.

64
00:04:07.838 --> 00:04:10.170
Then the syrup will freeze.

65
00:04:10.171 --> 00:04:15.508
The candy will be just like a chocolate-coated ice-cream cone!"

66
00:04:15.509 --> 00:04:21.042
"But the candy will still taste like vegetables," Molly pointed out.

67
00:04:21.043 --> 00:04:26.567
"Who cares?" said Caswell. "Let's start pouring!"

68
00:04:26.568 --> 00:04:30.410
We all took turns pouring the syrup.

69
00:04:30.411 --> 00:04:36.023
Caswell tried to be careful, but he got syrup all over his face.

70
00:04:36.024 --> 00:04:39.735
In fact, he got syrup all over everything.

71
00:04:39.736 --> 00:04:42.487
That was when Mom walked into my room.

72
00:04:42.488 --> 00:04:45.208
"Iggy!" she cried.

73
00:04:45.209 --> 00:04:51.719
"What do you think you're doing?"

